// PORT-PENDING 0504 crates-jet-codegen-src-codegen-tir-mod-slice-1: crates/jet-codegen/src/Codegen/TIR/mod.rs:1-1761
// Translate in place: replace the //RS lines below with the 1:1 Jet port (keep `// Rust: <file>:<line>` anchors).
//RS //! TIR — a small, *typed* intermediate representation for codegen (c109 Phase 1).
//RS //!
//RS //! ## Why this exists
//RS //!
//RS //! Today codegen (`emit_func` and friends) re-derives semantic facts while it
//RS //! emits Rust: it calls `expr_jet_ty` to re-infer expression types and
//RS //! `operand_is_integer` to re-decide which operator traps on overflow. That is
//RS //! exactly the "codegen re-derives / falls back" smell that invariant I3
//RS //! ("codegen is dumb") forbids, and it is the bug class that produced the I2
//RS //! holes the checked-IR effort was built to kill.
//RS //!
//RS //! The TIR is the fix. It is a distinct, post-sema representation whose defining
//RS //! property is **TOTALITY**: every fact codegen needs is carried concretely on
//RS //! the node — never re-inferred, never an `Option` codegen has to fall back from.
//RS //! Every `TExpr` carries its resolved `Type`; every `Binary` carries its
//RS //! overflow decision as a plain `bool`; every `Let` carries the resolved binding
//RS //! type. The borrowed `TFactChannel` below exposes the optimizer-relevant
//RS //! sema facts without allocating a side table or introducing another IR.
//RS //! Consumers treat an absent channel fact as "not proven" and keep the checked
//RS //! Prelude operation.
//RS //!
//RS //! The emitter (`emit_tir_func`) makes ZERO semantic decisions: it
//RS //! pattern-matches TIR fields and formats Rust. It never calls `expr_jet_ty` or
//RS //! `operand_is_integer`.
//RS 
//RS //!
//RS //! ## Coverage contract
//RS //!
//RS //! `tir_covers` proves that every reachable function is fully represented by TIR.
//RS //! TIR is the only codegen seam: a coverage miss is an internal compiler error,
//RS //! never a fallback. Add a node only when its construct is covered, and make every
//RS //! field total.
//RS 
//RS // Re-export the parent `Codegen` glob so the split-out submodules
//RS // (`subset`/`lower`/`emit`) reach `Cx`, `mangle`, `rust_*`, etc. via `use super::*`.
//RS pub(crate) use super::*;
